      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python/cpython/contents/Doc%2Fc-api%2Fintro.rst?ref=05e7f0977561a3f432db868eae4800cb3ab6be6f",
      "patch": "@@ -124,6 +124,9 @@ complete listing.\n    worse performances (due to increased code size for example). The compiler is\n    usually smarter than the developer for the cost/benefit analysis.\n \n+   If Python is :ref:`built in debug mode <debug-build>` (if the ``Py_DEBUG``\n+   macro is defined), the :c:macro:`Py_ALWAYS_INLINE` macro does nothing.\n+\n    It must be specified before the function return type. Usage::\n \n        static inline Py_ALWAYS_INLINE int random(void) { return 4; }"
    },
    {
      "sha": "d27d0838f1b2cb64646cb29fceb43b46a4094cf9",
      "filename": "Include/pyport.h",
      "status": "modified",
      "additions": 10,
      "deletions": 1,
      "changes": 11,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/05e7f0977561a3f432db868eae4800cb3ab6be6f/Include%2Fpyport.h",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/python/cpython/raw/05e7f0977561a3f432db868eae4800cb3ab6be6f/Include%2Fpyport.h",
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python/cpython/contents/Include%2Fpyport.h?ref=05e7f0977561a3f432db868eae4800cb3ab6be6f",
      "patch": "@@ -568,10 +568,19 @@ extern \"C\" {\n // worse performances (due to increased code size for example). The compiler is\n // usually smarter than the developer for the cost/benefit analysis.\n //\n+// If Python is built in debug mode (if the Py_DEBUG macro is defined), the\n+// Py_ALWAYS_INLINE macro does nothing.\n+//\n // It must be specified before the function return type. Usage:\n //\n //     static inline Py_ALWAYS_INLINE int random(void) { return 4; }\n-#if defined(__GNUC__) || defined(__clang__) || defined(__INTEL_COMPILER)\n+#if defined(Py_DEBUG)\n+   // If Python is built in debug mode, usually compiler optimizations are\n+   // disabled. In this case, Py_ALWAYS_INLINE can increase a lot the stack\n+   // memory usage. For example, forcing inlining using gcc -O0 increases the\n+   // stack usage from 6 KB to 15 KB per Python function call.\n+#  define Py_ALWAYS_INLINE\n+#elif defined(__GNUC__) || defined(__clang__) || defined(__INTEL_COMPILER)\n #  define Py_ALWAYS_INLINE __attribute__((always_inline))\n #elif defined(_MSC_VER)\n #  define Py_ALWAYS_INLINE __forceinline"
    }
  ],
